resets. The velocity *just after* the reset is $x_2^{new}$ and *just before* the
reset is $x_2^{old}$.                                                           
                                                                                
Since $x_1$ is continuous but $x_2$ is discontinuous at the reset, we look for  
points just before and just after the crossing. Due to discretization,          
$X_1[k-1]$ and $X_1[k]$ might both be on one side, or straddle zero.            
                                                                                
I will search for a clear sign change in $X_1$.                                 
                                                                                
